# __PROJECT_NAME__

_One line on what this project does and for whom._

Created from [project-template](https://github.com/sjmeehan9/project-template) and bootstrapped for the **__PLATFORM__** stack.

## Start here

- **`docs/project-profile.md`** — the stack contract every agent reads first: platform, validation tiers, test frameworks, run instructions, git workflow, human tasks, delivery posture. Keep it current.
- **`CLAUDE.md` / `AGENTS.md`** — session entry points for Claude Code and Codex.
- **`docs/`** — the documents the delivery pipelines produce and consume: requirements, brief, solution design, phase plan, component breakdowns, component overviews, test reports, team state.
- **`supporting-files/AGENT_FLOWS.md`** — how the agent pipeline fits together.

## Delivery pipelines

`validate-with-waitlist`, `build-with-agent-team-light`, and `build-with-agent-team` are installed as skills (`.claude/skills/`, `.agents/skills/`). Every run has a persistent Steward.

## Template updates

Agent definitions, skills, doctrine and tooling arrive through the weekly `template-sync` pull request (it needs the `TEMPLATE_SYNC_PAT` secret). Change them in `project-template`, not here: local edits to synced files are overwritten by the next sync. Files listed in `.templatesyncignore` (this README, `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `docs/`, application source, stack manifests) are project-owned and never touched by the sync.
